From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiron Builder <builder@chiron.local>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 18:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] w2: rate-limit scan payload buffer wrap diagnostics

The firmware reports enough scan-result payload to wrap the driver's bounded
scratch buffer during ordinary NetworkManager scans.  The existing wrap is
safe: it resets the offset before copying the next payload.  Logging it with
AML_INFO, however, floods the kernel journal while Wi-Fi remains connected.

Keep the proven existing wrap behaviour and demote its diagnostic to a
rate-limited debug message.  This preserves visibility for driver debugging
without presenting expected scan traffic as an error.
---
 aml_drv/fullmac/aml_rx.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/aml_drv/fullmac/aml_rx.c b/aml_drv/fullmac/aml_rx.c
index fff86e7..3fa8949 100644
--- a/aml_drv/fullmac/aml_rx.c
+++ b/aml_drv/fullmac/aml_rx.c
@@ -1501,7 +1501,7 @@ void aml_scan_rx(struct aml_hw *aml_hw, struct hw_rxhdr *hw_rxhdr, struct sk_bu
             /*scanres payload process end*/
             if (aml_hw->scanres_payload_buf_offset + le32_to_cpu(hw_rxhdr->hwvect.len) > SCAN_RESULTS_MAX_CNT*500) {
                 aml_hw->scanres_payload_buf_offset = 0;
-                AML_INFO("scanres_payload_buf overflow, flush");
+                pr_debug_ratelimited("aml_w2: scan result payload buffer wrapped\\n");
             }
             /*scanres payload process start*/
             memcpy(aml_hw->scanres_payload_buf + aml_hw->scanres_payload_buf_offset,
